erve that we have a diagram\n<MATH_0011>\nof morphisms of families of maps with fixed target of <MATH_0012>.\nThis diagram does not commute, but by Lemma <REF_0002>\nthe pullback functors on descent data one gets are canonically\nisomorphic. Hence <MATH_0013> and <MATH_0014>\npull back to isomorphic objects in <MATH_0015>.\nHence by assumption (3) we obtain an isomorphism\n<MATH_0016> in the category <MATH_0017>.\nWe omit the verification that these arrows are compatible\nwith the morphisms <MATH_0018>; hint: use the faithfulness\nof the functors in condition (4).\nWe also omit the verification that the functor\n<MATH_0019> is\nfully faithful.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7a29d4e9efc1911dc11c2fd7527638bae4fe291f71970c2f78343bdce73dd85f", "unit_id": "tag:0GEA:proof"}
